the wild cast of thor love and thunder  certainly had a crazy time filming the  whole movie they had so many favorite  scenes that it seems like they could  have just said the entire thing was  their favorite but for the purpose of  our own enjoyment we've gathered up a  bunch of their favorites and some of  their least favorites we think everyone  can agree though the music choice in  this one was perfect number one the  guardian team up we all dreamed to see  again and one of the best times for  chris hemsworth to be on set that's just  such a joy to work with that crew seeing  the continuation of the squad all the  way back from end game felt like bliss  for chris it felt to him like he was  having a little reunion with some old  classmates and these were the scenes in  love and thunder that thor could really  be himself pairing an offbeat superhero  with a couple of space outcasts what's  the perfect dynamic to open the movie  with number two one may think a  superhero should have epic action  sequences but director taika watiti  believes the character should have  epicness in a different aspect it's got  a great pair of essence the most talked  about scene from the film was chris  hemsworth's stunning nude physique  during thor's encounter with zeus not  that we were gawking or anything but it  was hard not to notice the demigod's  assets i'm very proud of it as well i'm  as proud of his  as he is being that this was a moment  taika really wanted in the film chris  was all too pleased to agree with him  hey chris  asking for a friend what's your method  to get those assets  number three as best buy falls out of  the mainstream its parking lots still  seem to thrive we were literally in a  parking lot with like a blue screen  natalie portman was stunned to walk on  set and see a big blue screen in front  of a best buy she thought where's the  punchline tyka but don't be fooled  natalie he's finding creative things in  the most unsuspecting of places one of  them was beautifully like beautiful  visually scenes i've seen on film this  scene was actually portman's favorite  once she saw how it turned out in the  final cut  number four poor christian bale has a  lot of his favorite scenes cut from this  film one most notable was a lovely  scream he got to do in the moment i did  not see the light of day as much as we  loved the throwbacks to classic music  videos 30 seconds of screaming may have  been a little too much on the audience's  ears  however if this bit isn't included in  the deleted scenes one day the gods will  have to pay for it  number five there are very few scenes in  this thor that the cast found  unfavorable and surprisingly one of the  most iconic moments in the film was  russell crowe's least favorite well  we'll see if i make it through the edit  he seemed a little too chillaxed about  the possibility of having his appearance  cut even though it was just too funny  for us watching his zeus interpretation  from an oscar-winning actor not being  pleased with your performance says a lot  but luckily the director listened to his  heart and kept him in  number six tessa thompson fans will know  that she has a special place in her  heart for goats and now she got to star  alongside two of them we had some we did  some press with a goat a goat actor her  and natalie held no shame in admitting  that they'd pet the prosthetic creatures  between takes and we really couldn't  blame them all that fuzz would turn into  nap time for us real quick but the one  thing portman admitted to and we hate  even saying this is that she got a  little too curious and started feeling  around the goats elsewhere you got  familiar with the time i did  i mean it was like kind of the first  thing i was curious about  number seven a marvel actor loving wire  work preposterous  i loved the wire work that's kind of the  most fun it seems like almost every  marvel actor despises the whole stunting  in the sky but natalie portman loved  being up on those harnesses and telling  jokes at the same time she couldn't  understand why a lot of these moments  were cut in the final edit but rest  assured why td knew what he was doing  and he was not so nice about it  you know if it was cut it's because  it wasn't good enough number eight a  super duo is a great team in films and  in real life that was the case for tessa  thompson and natalie portman who have  been friends for years thompson  expressed a lot of gratitude for being  in those scenes with jane growing as on  and off screen sisters in the process i  think you really get to see valkyrie  um find a sister again and and that is  is exciting her favorite bit was when  valkyrie and jane had that heart to  heart moment a great scene for them  and a wonderful break from all the chaos  for us number nine all that glitters  is not gold to take a water the gold  christian refers to here are the scenes  that he loved so much that were  unfortunately axed by the director  although he doesn't explain them in  detail he talks about them being a very  collaborative experience with taika and  quite possibly pushing the boundaries of  a family-friendly superhero movie he  understood in the end and after a great  debate with the director saying there's  so much gold that's on the cutting room  floor hilarious stuff and creepy stuff  but that was perhaps pushing it to a  realm where maybe it wouldn't have been  able to be family friendly which we  always wanted it to be  number 10 look out hulk we've got a real  life one on set just not filled with  gamma or anything tyga is more than just  a director it seems like he's more of a  hyper child set loose on a blockbuster  production he really enjoyed the scene  where new asgard sits in destruction  because  well he had the freedom to smash pieces  on set keep in mind being the director  of a huge marvel production can cause a  whole lot of stress so it looks like he  smashes set pieces a lot to keep calm  and cool during interviews it's always  good to let off a little steam like that  number 11 this was one of the many  scenes that were cut during the  post-production process  but what makes this one different is  that it was re-added during the final  edit all thanks to tessa the scene  portrays the actors at new asgard  begging valkyrie to put on another show  that doesn't seem like much of a scene  to us but to tessa this scene tugged at  her appreciation for theater strings she  explained her reasoning more saying i  was like that has to be in the movie  having them around to explore the  importance of theater and storytelling  as expressed in asgardian culture i just  loved that  number 12. you'd think a former batman  actor would have no problem with taking  on bigger foes but at the time of  filming love and thunder christian bale  was not embodying the buff batman  physique i'm a lot older than when i  last did any big fight sequences like  that he had just got done filming a  movie in which muscles were not to be  required  so he was just a little smaller than  usual one of his favorite scenes was  getting to face off against thor for the  first time although he found it quite  silly to be much smaller than his  co-star it really doesn't matter at all  with the size difference because bale  was having the time of his life beating  up a demigod  number 13 for the love of thunder let  hemsworth keep his shirt on we know a  lot of fans have no problem seeing a  shirtless thor waltz across the screen  but for the actor himself he did not  want to have a repeat of that in  ragnarok but what about in dark world  well he didn't have a problem going  shirtless for that film because he was  feeling top physical peakness from the  gym enough from us let's listen to what  chris had to say during an interview  this time around there wasn't one in the  script which i was really happy about  and then tychus said no i think we need  a shirt off scene i was like uh no we've  done that don't make me do it again  number 14. having a bad handle on your  superhero weapon can prove to cause  injury chris hemsworth may have had a  little too much liberty with his hammer  swings during the fight with hulk in  ragnarok and that case proved to be  destructive on that poor guy's noggin i  think i probably did more damage to  myself just kind of swinging the big  thing around  the way he recalled the situation or at  least remembers it is that when fighting  cgi you have to make a definitive choice  in where you're swinging do you think he  might have believed the hulk was on top  of his head or something  number 15 if one person in the mcu could  get away with slapping a literal demigod  it would have to be jane this scene was  a serious one for chris and natalie yet  natalie may have had more fun with it  than you'd think maybe i just wanted to  keep doing it over and over again  and i was intentionally messing up doing  multiple takes of the same slap seems a  little extra at first glance but being  that she is a whole foot smaller than  hemsworth makes for a hard slapping  angle for sure these were no contact  smacks but for chris it must have been a  little annoying to keep jerking your  head around  this goes to show that even the biggest  hollywood productions cut corners and  film at best buy parking lots from time  to time but this kind of filmmaking  hustle really created memorable moments  for this cast the favorite scenes  definitely outweighed the least favorite  and if they had a good time making it we  really had a great time watching it what  was your favorite scene from thor love  and thunder if it's that scene we won't  judge let us know in the comments
 

